WEBVTT

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.110
Hey, hurry up!

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:41.820
Wait!

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.070
Awesome.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:22.610
It's been a long time.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.440
I've come back.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.580
I'm back in my hometown.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:38.600
You're...

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.720
You're Himawari!

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.400
You've come back.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.910
You've become so pretty.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.910
Your grandma will be very happy.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.610
It's been a long time.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:03.660
Grandma, I'm home!

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.210
She's not here.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:43.970
Grandma?

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.430
Hayato-dono!

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.940
I followed you here.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:04:00.550
I offered to pay a long-distance truck driver for a ride...

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:05.580
but my last paycheck for night duty fell out through a hole in my wallet.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.970
I was beaten up and nearly sold to a foreign country.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.180
Then...

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.980
That's terrible.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.360
What a weird expression!

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:17.200
Do you mean Tarou? Or do you mean...

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.860
So that dog's called Tarou?

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.740
That... Um... Your childhood times were...

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:28.000
Could these pictures be...

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:35.220
I remember them saying that all of Hayato's memories from before primary school had been fabricated.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:36.790
That's true.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:40.330
The images just now were exactly like my memories.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:44.130
I'm sure Grandma knows something.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.590
But she's not here.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:51.380
You don't have to trust all the data that Kotarou brought, do you?

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:55.420
They may not always attack us with brute force.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:58.350
They might be planning to make us self-destruct from something like this.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:03.540
This reminds me of The Shinobis, 30th installment: The Episode of Teaching.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:08.750
Sometimes the enemy will not use strength or skill,

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:11.400
but will attack the weakness in one's heart.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.220
When one's heart is disturbed, one must be even more aware.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:17.020
One must look at all things calmly,
then the truth will come to light by itself.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:17.850
Right?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.860
I watched the DVDs.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.700
I had a lot of free time during night duty.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.850
Well, it was pretty interesting.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.370
Hayato-dono...

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.470
I'll hang around with you to verify your memories.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.210
I want to know the truth too.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.220
Yeah.

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:43.110
You got excited about the ice cream someone bought for you
and played around until you fell into the rice field?

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.780
I don't remember that.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.990
You ran away from a lion dance,

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:51.280
people thought you'd been kidnapped,
and that caused a huge fuss?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.680
Well, I think you remembered it incorrectly.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:02.260
The river overflowed because of a typhoon,

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:05.650
and all the villagers passed through here and took shelter in the neighboring village?

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:10.380
Such a strong typhoon hasn't passed through here in the past few decades.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:11.890
Why?

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.620
Why does nobody except me remember all the things that happened in this village?

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.300
This happens all the time.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:22.390
Maybe you watched the news on TV and turned it into your own memories?

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.240
Hayato-dono!

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.740
Himawari, thanks for saving me.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:44.140
Hayato-dono, thank goodness you're safe.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.520
Now I remember. I was saved once before.

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:01.270
There was a big water mill built next to a new canal.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:05.300
One day when I was playing there...

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.650
Open the water gate!

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:22.150
They opened the water gate completely, drained all the water behind the dam, and saved me.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:27.510
But because of that, the water gushing out from the gate damaged Grandma's house.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:31.140
If it was such a huge incident, then someone must remember it.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.830
But, I doubt that's true.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.530
Let's go and see.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.580
There <i>is a dam.</i>

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:41.850
Yes.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.540
But somehow it looks old.

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.940
Now that you've said it, you're right.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:50.580
Excuse me.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:52.900
Um...

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:56.120
This water mill was built not too long ago, right?

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:01.980
I think it was built by the
previous-previous-previous village head.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.460
I think that was about sixty years ago.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:07.250
S-Sixty years?

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.720
B-But I'm sure that I played around here.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:14.340
And you remembered that you nearly drowned here too.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.440
Yes.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:18.340
They opened the water gate completely and saved me.

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:23.410
If you did something like that, the old lady's house down there would've been flooded.

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:26.420
Oh, come to think of it, that <i>did happen.</i>

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:32.490
It happened when I was in primary school.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.940
That was about fifty years ago.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:45.170
Nobody remembers anymore.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.960
Everyone's just forgotten about it.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.360
We were just asking old folks.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:52.680
My memories...

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:54.730
Cheer up.

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:57.260
If we ask your grandma, I'm sure...

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.750
Could it be...

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.410
that Grandma too...

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:01.870
Hey, there...

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.960
There's a light in Grandma's house.

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:17.670
Grandma.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.440
Welcome back, Himawari.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:26.410
When I went to the farm in the mountains,
the villagers said that they'd seen you,

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:27.950
so I hurried back.

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:27.950
Grandma!

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:29.740
Oh dear, oh dear...

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:33.150
What's wrong, my dear girl?

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.120
This is Marikouji Hayato-sensei.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.680
He's my homeroom teacher at Shinobi High.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:40.690
Hello.

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:41.470
Teacher?

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.260
Why did you suddenly come back with a teacher?

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:45.240
Uh...

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.310
Well...

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.620
It must be a home visit, right?

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:52.320
Thank you so much for your trouble.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:54.610
I'm heating the bath water right now.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.210
I'd like my bath to be thirty eight degrees, please.

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:05.000
Is this what Himawari knitted for me?

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:08.550
So, how does it look?

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:11.260
It's very cute, Grandma.

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:14.550
I ran out of yarn, so the color changed.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:21.560
Something like that happened with the watermelon I sent.

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:25.240
Shinobi High sounds like a fun school.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:28.860
Her classmates are even more fun.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:31.190
There's an herbal freak, a miso soup princess,

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:32.950
a spy with nothing but false reports,

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:34.730
a violent "arinsu" girl,

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:38.600
and a girl with a kappa boyfriend and a farting dog.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.070
You're just saying whatever you feel like.

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:45.520
And that weird dog always laughs "ushishishi"...

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.520
We had one too: Tarou.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.430
Tarou?

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:50.430
Oh, Tarou!

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:55.070
He became lonely easily, so he always followed me around.

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:59.030
He also sneaked in and curled up between us at bedtime.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:03.730
Yes, yes. He got lonely easily and liked pickled radishes a lot.

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:04.420
That's right.

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:06.290
But when I was four...

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.900
Tarou won't wake up.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:10.380
Why?

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:12.270
Everyone prayed for him.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.640
I haven't been to visit his grave for a long time.

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:19.030
Um... The grave is...

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.660
In the forest out back.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:22.420
Yup. The forest out back.

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:25.620
What's up with this girl, suddenly bringing up all of this?

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:29.230
I remembered when I was looking at your pictures during the day.

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:30.350
Where are the albums?

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:31.950
I put them away.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.620
Really, you made such a mess.

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:35.360
Let's look at the albums.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:37.110
I want to talk about old times.

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:45.450
It's sour!

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:46.970
But it's delicious.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:52.920
It's dried in sunlight and pickled with kelp,
and then dried in sunlight again.

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:55.230
That's just the drying process.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.330
Shall I bring out the ones that are properly finished?

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:00.330
Can I have them?

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:02.230
There.

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:03.870
So many!

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:06.190
It's fine. It's fine.

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:10.130
If there are too many, then share them with the other teachers.

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:14.010
Speaking of teachers, there are lots of weird ones.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.840
Hey! Himawari!

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.180
Hayato-dono.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:53.800
See?

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:55.190
It's here.

00:12:58.580 --> 00:12:59.580
It's real.

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:00.740
Relax.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:01.980
Let's go already.

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:03.390
It's creepy here.

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:08.850
Himawari?

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:20.400
Grandma.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.020
I've been preparing.

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:24.880
I knew this day would come.

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:29.720
Himawari. That was the first time I lied to you.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.630
It's an old story.

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:43.690
After losing my son and his wife in a plane crash,

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:49.850
I lost my will to live and just continued to exist day by day.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:55.220
Raise a child?

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:56.990
It's a five-year-old.

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:59.180
We'll provide her living expenses.

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:00.700
That's so sudden.

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.890
Why did you choose me?

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:07.760
It's one of the country's secret projects.

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:13.080
You were chosen as the person most suitable for raising the child.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.020
Whose child is she actually?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:18.460
The girl is the government's child.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:22.270
She'll be working for the country someday.

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:24.330
For the country?

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:26.800
Please don't try to make any unnecessary inquiries.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.030
Here are the documents.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:33.850
They prove that she's been your grandchild since she was born.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:37.490
Please raise her with love, as you normally would.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:56.850
Strangely, the child's memories were shown there,

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:58.990
and for the child's sake,

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:06.400
my memories were fabricated too, as my son's daughter.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:19.620
I, who had been completely alone, and a child with no relatives.

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:25.740
This could be a gift from God, a destined meeting.

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:30.640
Of course, I had my anxieties.

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:32.260
Would everything be all right?

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:37.870
Could I raise this unknown child properly?

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:49.500
But the villagers believed that she was my son's child
and that I had taken her in from a relative.

00:15:53.020 --> 00:15:58.250
She cried and laughed, and she kept me busy.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:02.400
But she grew up quickly and healthily.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:16.880
Himawari!

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:20.870
I'll bring her back.

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:28.200
Wait! Himawari!

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:37.480
I'm sorry, Himawari.

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:41.200
I'm sorry.

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:50.790
Damn it. I can't catch up to her.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.510
But...

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:56.740
This will do it.

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:05.340
Hayato-dono.

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:06.810
O-Ouch...

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:07.740
Himawari.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.970
Let me go!

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:16.780
Everyone lied to me!

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:18.330
Even Grandma!

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:20.420
Even though I believed in her.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.560
Himawari, calm down.

00:17:32.390 --> 00:17:33.790
Hayato-dono...

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:37.360
Sour...

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.280
It's the plum that your grandma pickled.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:40.730
Listen, Himawari.

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:42.020
This sourness...

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:43.900
is real.

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:48.960
You grew up eating this, right?

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.120
You didn't grow up alone.

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:54.040
No matter how you were born,

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:56.750
the love your grandma feels for you hasn't changed!

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:19.110
You understand your grandma's feelings, don't you?

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:20.500
Yes.

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.770
All right. Then let's go home.

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:34.360
I'm sorry if my question is rude, but were you carrying all that while chasing me?

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:39.120
I-It's a habit leftover from when I had no food. I can't let go of food I've been given.

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:47.550
What is it?

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:50.770
There's an evil flame in your eyes.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.980
T-This is bad!

00:18:58.460 --> 00:18:59.820
Grandma!

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:09.890
What happened?

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:12.540
By the time I'd noticed it, the fire had spread.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.150
Thank goodness you're okay.

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:16.280
What should we do?

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:22.050
If you did something like that, the old lady's house down there would've been flooded.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.930
I'm going to let the water out.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:29.600
Take care of Grandma.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.490
Oh! Then at least... I must...

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:35.350
What are you doing?

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:44.410
Grandma! Grandma!

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.450
Where are you?

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.530
Grandma!

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:55.930
Grandma!

00:19:55.930 --> 00:19:57.270
Where are you?

00:19:58.510 --> 00:19:59.710
There she is.

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:04.950
The fire's spreading fast!

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:06.350
Anyway, hurry up!

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:14.940
I did it!

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:39.590
Grandma!

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:40.420
Hayato-dono!

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:43.130
We're saved.

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:46.730
It's a re-enactment of the incident fifty years ago.

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:52.100
Yup. I almost drowned in the dam up there.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:55.010
That was your memory?

00:20:57.720 --> 00:20:58.710
Oh no!

00:20:58.710 --> 00:21:00.800
We have to shut the gate.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:08.720
Grandma, are you all right?

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:09.800
Yes.

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:12.980
Thank goodness I brought along Shikimi-san's medicine.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:15.870
No matter what, I'm glad you're all right.

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:18.150
But all she was able to save was...

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:23.590
Isn't it a beautiful white kimono?

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:26.900
She put her life on the line for Himawari-chan.

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:34.000
I think you'll do it someday.

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:38.710
Grandma, a ninja is forbidden to love.

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:42.010
That's the iron rule.

00:21:42.850 --> 00:21:45.730
It's not a problem if nobody knows.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:47.450
Right, Sensei?

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:48.140
Yes.

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:51.390
Let's break watermelons in the summer, and pound rice cakes in the winter.

00:22:05.870 --> 00:22:07.070
Aren't we lucky?

00:22:07.070 --> 00:22:09.000
It didn't burn up.

00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:10.080
Yes.

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:12.960
We can just start over.

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:16.400
We can make as many memories as we want from now on, right?

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:22.390
Hayato-dono, what are you thinking about?

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:27.100
Actually, it's something I found out after you left the school.

00:22:27.590 --> 00:22:30.040
Your grandma's story proved it.

00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:34.690
The government sold the project to a civilian company after that.

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:37.130
You mean... that pharmaceutical company.

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:41.460
I have to go find out about my past too.

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:44.320
Let's find out the truth.

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:45.920
Will you come with me?

00:22:46.270 --> 00:22:48.150
I'll follow you wherever you go.

00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:58.640
I'll be waiting for you. Come back any time!

00:24:11.580 --> 00:24:14.370
A village was burned down to cinders,

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:19.200
and an infuriated leader and Wabisuke-kun were there.

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:21.350
Who did this?

00:24:22.440 --> 00:24:26.820
The ones who attacked the village were Kyuuri-sensei and Fudenoko-sensei?

00:24:26.820 --> 00:24:29.440
Why? Why? Why?!

00:24:29.440 --> 00:24:31.650
Even though we're all ninja comrades.

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:33.020
Next time:

00:24:33.020 --> 00:24:35.390
"A past of secrecy is a tricky pattern."

00:24:35.800 --> 00:24:39.000
Hayato-dono, all the mysteries have been solved.
